      "writtenOn": "2023-02-13T17:56:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Motivation: Yes -- adding in and plumbing a SkColorType that has extremely limited implementation feels like something we should avoid if we can.\n\nAs for compute: It should be exactly the same work either way. The codec logic that\u0027s been added is going to do a decode to 8888, then invoke skcms to do a format + colorspace conversion. Alternately, you can ask the codec to decode to 8888, then invoke skcms to do a format + colorspace conversion. I think the cost is identical.",
      "parentUuid": "9935ae8f_5b9e4ba8",
      "revId": "0a7cc58e0f16eff164eb56742b09c8c4da82551f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
